## Slash Commands

The installed `pi-subagents` package also exposes user-facing slash commands.
Use these when the direct `subagent` tool is not callable in the current harness or when the work is easier to launch interactively.

### Available commands
- `/run <agent> <task>` — run one agent
- `/chain ...` — sequential multi-agent pipeline
- `/parallel ...` — concurrent multi-agent execution
- `/agents` — open the Agents Manager TUI
- `/subagents-status` — inspect active and recent async runs

### Examples
```text
/run debugger Investigate why login fails in production
/run reviewer Review this diff --fork

/chain scout "scan the codebase" -> planner "create implementation plan"
/chain scout "analyze auth" -> planner -> worker --bg

/parallel scout "audit frontend" -> reviewer "audit backend"
/parallel scout "scan frontend" -> scout "scan backend" -> scout "scan infra" --bg
```

### Important note
For this skill, prefer documenting and invoking the **tool schema** when instructing the model. The slash commands are still useful because they reflect real package capabilities and provide the fallback path when the direct tool is unavailable in the current harness.

