## Common Options

| Option | Purpose | Example |
|--------|---------|---------|
| `agent` | Which agent to run | `"debugger"`, `"researcher"` |
| `task` | What to ask the agent | `"Fix the bug"` |
| `model` | Override model | `"MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.5"` |
| `output` | Write result to file | `"result.md"` |
| `skill` | Pass skill(s) to the agent | `["commit"]` |
| `async` | Run in background | `true` |
| `cwd` | Working directory | `"/path/to/project"` |
| `context` | Execution context mode | `"fresh"` or `"fork"` |
| `agentScope` | Control agent discovery | `"user"`, `"project"`, `"both"` |
| `clarify` | Show/edit execution plan in TUI first | `true` |

### Important runtime notes
- `context` defaults to `"fresh"`.
- `context: "fork"` runs from a real branch of the parent session instead of a clean session.
- `agentScope: "both"` is the practical default; project agents override user agents on name collision.
- For curated implementation and review workflows, `agentScope: "user"` is often the better choice because it avoids accidental project-level prompt overrides.

